<title>DENMARK: MAERSK FINDS N.SEA TEST BORE UNVIABLE.</title>
<headline>MAERSK FINDS N.SEA TEST BORE UNVIABLE.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Test drilling in the Danish North Sea by Maersk Oil and Gas has ended without the discovery of viable quantities of oil, the Danish Energy Agency said on Thursdsay.</p>
<p>An agency statement said that drilling, at the NW Adda-1 site, showed traces of oil but no grounds to begin test production.</p>
<p>&quot;Drilling has now been permanently closed down,&quot; it said. --Stig Oerskov Pedersen, Copenhagen newsroom (45) 33969659</p>
</text>
